# Overview
Purpose, target users, product context, and core visual direction.

# Brand
Approved logo usage, brand assets, tone, and non-negotiable brand constraints.

# Colors
Semantic color tokens:
- Primary / Secondary
- Background / Surface / Elevated Surface
- Text Primary / Text Muted / Inverse Text
- Border / Divider
- Status: Success, Warning, Danger, Info

# Typography
Font families, type scale, weights, line heights, and heading/body hierarchy.

# Spacing and Layout
Spacing scale, grid system, container max-widths, and breakpoints.

# Components
Core UI primitives and interaction states (default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, error):
- Buttons
- Inputs & Forms
- Cards & Containers
- Tables & Data Displays
- Navigation & Modals/Dialogs

# Accessibility
Semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, visible focus rings, WCAG contrast targets, form labels/errors, and reduced motion support.

# Responsive Behavior
Layout adaptation rules for mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports.

# Do Not
Patterns, visual overrides, or styling shortcuts that must not be introduced in this project.
